      "writtenOn": "2016-04-01T20:56:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This works with both relative and absolute paths. This is how os.path join operation works:\n\n\u003e\u003e\u003e os.path.join(\"/etc/keystone\", \"x/y/z\")\n\n\u0027/etc/keystone/x/y/z\u0027\n\n\u003e\u003e\u003e os.path.join(\"/etc/keystone\", \"/x/y/z\")\n\n\u0027/x/y/z\u0027\n\nThe \"s.startswith(\u0027/\u0027)\" filter condition has been added as a simple sanity check.",
